<h1>Gemma 4 31B-IT Deployment Analysis via AEX Model Service</h1>

<table style="width:60%; margin-bottom:20pt;">
<tr><td style="width:40%; font-weight:bold; background:#E8E8E8;">User Story</td><td>2748133 - Explore deployment of Gemma model</td></tr>
<tr><td style="font-weight:bold; background:#E8E8E8;">Model</td><td>google/gemma-4-31b-it</td></tr>
<tr><td style="font-weight:bold; background:#E8E8E8;">Sprint</td><td>Cat Digital 2026 | Sprint 12 (Jun 10 - Jun 23)</td></tr>
<tr><td style="font-weight:bold; background:#E8E8E8;">Owner</td><td>Sowndarya Kurapati</td></tr>
<tr><td style="font-weight:bold; background:#E8E8E8;">Date</td><td>June 18, 2026</td></tr>
<tr><td style="font-weight:bold; background:#E8E8E8;">Region</td><td>us-east-2 (Ohio)</td></tr>
<tr><td style="font-weight:bold; background:#E8E8E8;">Pricing Type</td><td>On-Demand</td></tr>
</table>


<h2>1. Model Specifications</h2>
<table>
<tr><th>Specification</th><th>Value</th></tr>
<tr><td>Model Name</td><td>google/gemma-4-31b-it</td></tr>
<tr><td>Parameters</td><td>31 Billion (Dense)</td></tr>
<tr><td>Model Size on Disk (BF16)</td><td>~65 GB</td></tr>
<tr><td>VRAM Required (FP16/BF16)</td><td>~71 GB</td></tr>
<tr><td>VRAM Required (NVFP4 Quantized)</td><td>~45 GB</td></tr>
<tr><td>Minimum GPU</td><td>1x NVIDIA A100 80GB (single GPU) or 2x A100 40GB (tensor parallel)</td></tr>
<tr><td>Recommended Serving Engine</td><td>vLLM v0.8.0+</td></tr>
<tr><td>Context Length</td><td>Up to 256K tokens</td></tr>
<tr><td>Source</td><td>JFrog Artifactory (artifacts.cat.com) - Approved</td></tr>
<tr><td>Artifactory Path</td><td>cat-huggingface-repo/models/google/gemma-4-31B-it/</td></tr>
</table>

<h2>2. AEX Model Service - All Supported Deployment Paths</h2>
<p>The CMAAI-Model-Service GitHub Actions workflow (cmaai-model-service.yaml) supports <strong>5 model-type options</strong>. Below is the feasibility assessment of each for Gemma 4 31B:</p>
<table>
<tr><th>#</th><th>model-type</th><th>Description</th><th>Can Deploy Gemma 4 31B?</th><th>Primary Blocker</th></tr>
<tr><td>1</td><td><strong>sagemaker</strong></td><td>Deploy via Amazon SageMaker endpoint</td><td class="warn">MAYBE (best chance)</td><td>65 GB tar.gz packaging; no GPU instance selection</td></tr>
<tr><td>2</td><td><strong>huggingface</strong></td><td>Deploy HuggingFace model on AEX infrastructure</td><td class="fail">NO</td><td>Storage 20 GiB &lt; 65 GB; No GPU on Fargate; ECR 52 GB limit</td></tr>
<tr><td>3</td><td><strong>llmobject</strong></td><td>Deploy LLM object (likely LLM-specific path)</td><td class="warn">UNKNOWN - Needs Investigation</td><td>Undocumented; may support larger models</td></tr>
<tr><td>4</td><td><strong>mlflow</strong></td><td>Deploy MLflow-packaged model</td><td class="fail">NO</td><td>Wrong model format (not MLflow)</td></tr>
<tr><td>5</td><td><strong>pythonpackage</strong></td><td>Deploy Python package model</td><td class="fail">NO</td><td>Wrong model format + same infra limits</td></tr>
</table>


<h2>3. PATH 1: model-type = "sagemaker" (Most Viable)</h2>
<h3>How It Works</h3>
<p>Model is packaged as model.tar.gz, uploaded to S3, and deployed to a SageMaker real-time inference endpoint via the CMAAI-Model-Service workflow.</p>
<h3>Workflow Inputs Required</h3>
<table>
<tr><th>Input</th><th>Value for Gemma 4 31B</th></tr>
<tr><td>environment</td><td>datahub-dev</td></tr>
<tr><td>model-name</td><td>gemma-4-31b-it</td></tr>
<tr><td>model-version</td><td>v1</td></tr>
<tr><td>model-type</td><td>sagemaker</td></tr>
<tr><td>sagemaker-model-artifact-filename</td><td>model.tar.gz</td></tr>
<tr><td>sagemaker-requirements-filename</td><td>requirements.txt</td></tr>
<tr><td>deploy-on-gpu</td><td>true</td></tr>
<tr><td>artifact-location</td><td>s3://pfn-aex-cmaai-mr-s3-bucket-dev/models/google/gemma-4-31b-it/model.tar.gz</td></tr>
<tr><td>network-type</td><td>routable</td></tr>
</table>

<h3>Feasibility Assessment</h3>
<table>
<tr><th>Requirement</th><th>SageMaker Capability</th><th>Gemma 4 31B Needs</th><th>Status</th></tr>
<tr><td>Model packaging (tar.gz)</td><td>S3 multipart upload, no hard size limit</td><td>65 GB tar.gz</td><td class="warn">POSSIBLE but very slow</td></tr>
<tr><td>Storage on endpoint</td><td>Configurable EBS volume</td><td>65+ GB</td><td class="pass">PASS</td></tr>
<tr><td>GPU availability</td><td>Multiple GPU instance families</td><td>A100 80GB minimum for FP16</td><td class="pass">PASS</td></tr>
<tr><td>Cold start</td><td>Instance launch + model load</td><td>5-15 minutes total</td><td class="warn">SLOW but acceptable</td></tr>
<tr><td>Inference timeout</td><td>Up to 60 seconds (real-time)</td><td>Depends on output length</td><td class="warn">RISK for long outputs</td></tr>
<tr><td>Gemma 4 on JumpStart</td><td>Available since April 2026</td><td>Pre-configured</td><td class="pass">CONFIRMED</td></tr>
</table>

<h3>Problems Blocking This Path</h3>
<table>
<tr><th>#</th><th>Problem</th><th>Detail</th><th>Severity</th></tr>
<tr><td>1</td><td class="fail">No staging infrastructure for 65 GB file operations</td><td>Need a server to: download from JFrog (65 GB) + compress to tar.gz + upload to S3. No such server exists. Cannot do this on a laptop.</td><td>CRITICAL</td></tr>
<tr><td>2</td><td class="fail">65 GB tar.gz packaging is impractical</td><td>Compressing 65 GB of safetensors files takes hours and produces an archive nearly as large (safetensors don't compress well).</td><td>HIGH</td></tr>
<tr><td>3</td><td class="warn">No GPU instance type selection in workflow</td><td>Workflow has deploy-on-gpu=true/false but no way to specify WHICH instance (ml.p4d.24xlarge, ml.g5.12xlarge). The model needs specific GPU types with enough VRAM.</td><td>HIGH</td></tr>
<tr><td>4</td><td class="warn">No JFrog to S3 automated transfer</td><td>Model sits in JFrog Artifactory. No pipeline exists to move it to the AEX S3 bucket. Lambda is limited to 10 GB. Would need ECS task or EC2 instance.</td><td>HIGH</td></tr>
<tr><td>5</td><td class="warn">SageMaker 60-second inference timeout</td><td>Real-time endpoints timeout at 60 seconds. Long-form generation may exceed this.</td><td>MEDIUM</td></tr>
</table>


