<h2>5. PATH 3: model-type = "llmobject" (Needs Investigation)</h2>
<h3>How It Works</h3>
<p><strong>Unknown.</strong> This model-type likely provides a specialized deployment path for Large Language Models. It may have different infrastructure requirements than the generic "huggingface" path.</p>
<h3>What We Know</h3>
<table>
<tr><th>Question</th><th>Answer</th></tr>
<tr><td>What infrastructure does it use?</td><td class="warn">UNKNOWN - needs team input</td></tr>
<tr><td>Does it support GPU?</td><td class="warn">UNKNOWN - needs team input</td></tr>
<tr><td>What storage limits apply?</td><td class="warn">UNKNOWN - needs team input</td></tr>
<tr><td>Does it support 65+ GB models?</td><td class="warn">UNKNOWN - needs team input</td></tr>
<tr><td>Is tensor parallelism supported?</td><td class="warn">UNKNOWN - needs team input</td></tr>
</table>
<h3>Action Required</h3>
<p>Ask the AEX team: "What does the <code>llmobject</code> model-type do? What infrastructure does it deploy to? Does it support 65+ GB models with GPU inference?"</p>
<p>This could potentially be the correct path for Gemma 4 31B if it was designed to handle LLM-specific requirements (large model size, GPU inference, tensor parallelism).</p>

<h2>6. PATH 4: model-type = "mlflow"</h2>
<h3>Why It Cannot Work</h3>
<table>
<tr><th>Reason</th><th>Detail</th></tr>
<tr><td class="fail">Wrong model format</td><td>Gemma 4 31B is a HuggingFace model with safetensors weights. It is NOT packaged as an MLflow model. MLflow is designed for traditional ML models (sklearn, XGBoost, PyTorch custom) or requires wrapping the model in an MLflow-compatible format.</td></tr>
<tr><td class="fail">Same infrastructure limits apply</td><td>Even if wrapped in MLflow format, the same storage (20 GiB) and GPU (no Fargate GPU) limitations would block deployment.</td></tr>
</table>

<h2>7. PATH 5: model-type = "pythonpackage"</h2>
<h3>Why It Cannot Work</h3>
<table>
<tr><th>Reason</th><th>Detail</th></tr>
<tr><td class="fail">Wrong model format</td><td>Gemma 4 31B is not a Python package. It is a 65 GB neural network with safetensors weight files. You cannot pip-install a 65 GB model.</td></tr>
<tr><td class="fail">Same infrastructure limits apply</td><td>Even if packaged as a Python module, the same storage (20 GiB) and GPU (no Fargate GPU) limitations would block deployment.</td></tr>
</table>


<h2>8. Complete Gap Analysis - Problems Preventing Deployment</h2>
<table>
<tr><th>#</th><th>Gap / Problem</th><th>Affects Path(s)</th><th>Current State</th><th>Required for Gemma 4 31B</th><th>Priority</th></tr>
<tr><td>1</td><td>Worker ephemeral storage too small</td><td>huggingface, pythonpackage, mlflow</td><td>20 GiB default</td><td>100+ GiB</td><td class="fail">P0 - CRITICAL</td></tr>
<tr><td>2</td><td>No JFrog to S3 automated transfer</td><td>sagemaker, huggingface (all paths)</td><td>Manual download only</td><td>Automated pipeline for 65+ GB</td><td class="fail">P0 - CRITICAL</td></tr>
<tr><td>3</td><td>ECR image layer limit = 52 GB</td><td>huggingface</td><td>52 GB max per layer (AWS hard limit)</td><td>Runtime S3 pull instead of baking into image</td><td class="fail">P0 - CRITICAL</td></tr>
